IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`
IMPORT `g1-art2-governor-misconduct`
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`
IMPORT `g8-nouns`

-- int-nouns.l4: the nouns of the integration layer, and nothing else.  `domain.l4` is untouched (no edit to it was needed: see NOTES.md, "Nouns requests").
-- A noun is here only because two or more of the integration layer's functions share it; the nouns a single headline needs are declared beside that headline.
-- Every name is a phrase no group uses ("... in the case"), so that the integration layer's names are unique across the fleet.

§ `Integration layer -- the nouns`

-- One person who may be a governor of the body: the facts Article 2(7) reads (group G1) and the facts Article 19(1) reads (group G6).
DECLARE `Person in the case` HAS
    considered IS A `Person considered as a governor` @desc The person as group G1 reads a governor: the person's record and the facts about the person's role in the body (Article 2(7))
    `facts for the reportable matters` IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` @desc The facts that decide which kinds of reportable matter describe the person (Article 19(1))
    `made a report under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has made a report of a reportable matter under Article 19(2) (read for Article 19(5): the declarations of the governors who have not reported)
    `provided a declaration of no reportable matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has provided a declaration under Article 19(3) or (4) that there is no reportable matter (read for Article 19(5))
    `reported matter awaiting determination` IS A MAYBE `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` @desc The person's reported matter and where the Commissioner has got to with it (Article 19(9)); NOTHING if the person has reported nothing

-- A body as the headline functions take it: the facts the Parts after Article 2 read about the entity, before any of them is derived.
-- The kinds of entity, Jersey-entity status and governors are DERIVED from these facts by group G1 (IP5), and each governor's reportable matters by group G6 (IP21); they are not asked for twice.
DECLARE `Body in the case` HAS
    name IS A STRING @desc The entity's name; the registered name once it is registered
    standing IS A `Standing on the register` @desc Where the entity stands on the register on the day asked (an input: the register is the Commissioner's record)
    purposes IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` @desc All of the entity's purposes (Article 2(6)) with the facts Article 6(2) reads about each; the entity's purposes are these purposes, in this order
    facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body that Article 2(1) and 2(3) read; its field `governors` is ignored (the governors are derived from `people`)
    model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` @desc The facts about the model constitution that Article 2(8) reads
    people IS A LIST OF `Person in the case` @desc Everyone who may be a governor; group G1 decides which of them are (Article 2(7))

-- One service of a required steps notice, with the dates on which its service is fixed by Article 38 (IP34).
DECLARE `Notice served in the case` HAS
    recipient IS A `Recipient of a required steps notice` @desc Whom the notice was served on (Article 27(3))
    belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief under Article 27(1) that the notice rests on
    `date sent` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the notice was sent
    `date received` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The date on which the notice was received, if known
    `date fixed by an Order under Article 38` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The date of service fixed by an Order under Article 38, if one fixes it
    time IS A `Time specified in a notice` @desc The time the notice specifies for the steps (Article 27(2)): a date or a period of days
    requirements IS A LIST OF `Requirement in a required steps notice` @desc The requirements the notice contains
    `the steps required have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the steps the notice requires have been taken

-- The facts the charity test reads (Article 5), apart from the entity and its purposes.
DECLARE `Facts for the charity test in the case` HAS
    `constitution facts` IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` @desc What the entity's constitution expressly permits as to control by a Minister, a member of the States Assembly or an equivalent (Article 5(2))
    `public benefit determination` IS A `Determination of public benefit` @desc Who determined the public benefit and what the determination found and did (Article 7)
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2) for the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order of the Minister under Article 5(3) disapplies the bar of Article 5(2) for this entity

-- generated by gen_replace.py: a copy of `Facts about the body under Article 2` (module g1-art2-entity) with the field `governors` replaced
GIVEN original IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The record to copy
      replacement IS A LIST OF Governor @desc The new value of the field `governors`
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`Int the facts about the body with the governors` original replacement MEANS
    `Facts about the body under Article 2` WITH
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust` IS original's `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust`
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` IS original's `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
        `a body corporate` IS original's `a body corporate`
        `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS original's `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
        `established under the law of Jersey` IS original's `established under the law of Jersey`
        `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862` IS original's `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862`
        `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009` IS original's `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009`
        `established by an enactment` IS original's `established by an enactment`
        `established by Act of the States` IS original's `established by Act of the States`
        `established by Royal Charter` IS original's `established by Royal Charter`
        `established in relation to Jersey` IS original's `established in relation to Jersey`
        `the Law by which the body corporate was established` IS original's `the Law by which the body corporate was established`
        `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS original's `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
        `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS original's `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
        `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey` IS original's `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey`
        `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` IS original's `the enactment under which the body was incorporated`
        `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons` IS original's `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons`
        `a partnership` IS original's `a partnership`
        `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to` IS original's `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to`
        `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS original's `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey`
        `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey` IS original's `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey`
        `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls` IS original's `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls`
        `governors` IS replacement

-- A notice of a decision (of the Commissioner, of the tribunal), with the dates that fix its service under Article 38 (IP34): the appeal period of Article 36(2) and the effect of a deregistration run from it.
DECLARE `Notice of a decision in the case` HAS
    `date sent` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the notice of the decision was sent
    `date received` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The date on which it was received, if known
    `date fixed by an Order under Article 38` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The date of service fixed by an Order under Article 38, if one fixes it

